<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins U.S. California turbine order.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins U.S. California turbine order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom, a venture between Britain's General Electric Co Plc and France's Alcatel Alsthom, said on Monday it had won a U.S. order worth about $60 million, or 38 million stg, for steam turbine modules.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the order, from Southern California Edison, was for new steam turbine modules at the San Onofre nuclear generating station.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
